<body><div class=WordSection1>
<div class="brand">📚 ENGLISH CODING · 영어코딩</div>
<h1>🦙 Functions Extension · 64 Cages — English Worksheet</h1>
<p><strong>Topic:</strong> One function, three loops · <strong>Course:</strong> Functions &amp; Games · <strong>Level:</strong> Extension (after helper functions) · <strong>Time:</strong> about 45 minutes</p>
<p>Last time one function built one cage. This time the same function builds <strong>64</strong>, stacked in a <strong>4 × 4 × 4</strong> tower. Every cage holds an animal and stands on grass.</p>
<p>Your cage from last lesson:</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">def make_cage(x: number, y: number, z: number, animal: number):
    blocks.fill(OAK_FENCE,
        pos(x, y, z),
        pos(x + 4, y + 3, z + 4), FillOperation.HOLLOW)
    blocks.fill(GRASS,
        pos(x, y, z),
        pos(x + 4, y, z + 4), FillOperation.REPLACE)
    mobs.spawn(animal, pos(x + 2, y + 1, z + 2))
</code></pre>
<p>One cage is <strong>5 wide, 4 tall, 5 deep</strong>.</p>
<hr />
<h2>1 · Predict 🔮</h2>
<p>Read each one. Write the number <strong>and the reason</strong>.</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">for col in range(4):
    make_cage(col * 6, 0, 0, LLAMA)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>How many cages? Which way do they run?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<pre><code class="language-python">for row in range(4):
    for col in range(4):
        make_cage(col * 6, 0, row * 6, LLAMA)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>How many cages now? What shape do they make?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<pre><code class="language-python">for level in range(4):
    for row in range(4):
        for col in range(4):
            make_cage(col * 6, level * 5, row * 6, LLAMA)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>How many cages? Which loop lifts them off the ground?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>A cage is 4 tall. The levels are 5 apart. What would happen if you changed <code>level * 5</code> to <code>level * 3</code>?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<hr />
<h2>2 · Spot the Bug 🐛</h2>
<p>Each one runs. Each one is wrong. Fix it, then say why.</p>
<p><strong>Bug A</strong> — This should build 64 cages. You count 16.</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">for row in range(4):
    for col in range(4):
        make_cage(col * 6, 0, row * 6, LLAMA)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Write the fix:</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Why was it wrong?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Bug B</strong> — Every animal disappears the moment the cage appears.</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">def make_cage(x: number, y: number, z: number, animal: number):
    mobs.spawn(animal, pos(x + 2, y + 1, z + 2))
    blocks.fill(OAK_FENCE,
        pos(x, y, z),
        pos(x + 4, y + 3, z + 4), FillOperation.HOLLOW)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Write the fix:</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Why was it wrong?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Bug C</strong> — All 64 cages land in one flat layer, cutting through each other.</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">for level in range(4):
    for row in range(4):
        for col in range(4):
            make_cage(col * 6, 0, row * 6, LLAMA)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Write the fix:</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<p><strong>Why was it wrong?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<hr />
<h2>3 · Read the Grid 🧊</h2>
<p>Each loop owns one direction.</p>
<div style="page-break-inside:avoid;break-inside:avoid;margin:14px 0">
