<p><strong>The last row is the far top corner. How far is that cage from where you stand?</strong></p>
<p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p><p class="ruled">&nbsp;</p>

<hr />
<h2>4 · Build It 🧱</h2>
<p>Stand somewhere with open space above you and behind you. The tower needs about <strong>20 blocks</strong> in each direction.</p>
<p>Fill the blanks and run it:</p>
<pre><code class="language-python">def make_cage(x: number, y: number, z: number, animal: number):
    blocks.fill(OAK_FENCE,
        pos(x, y, z),
        pos(x + 4, y + 3, z + 4), FillOperation.HOLLOW)
    blocks.fill(GRASS,
        pos(______, ______, ______),
        pos(x + 4, ______, z + 4), FillOperation.REPLACE)
    mobs.spawn(______, pos(x + 2, y + 1, z + 2))

for level in range(______):
    for row in range(______):
        for col in range(______):
            make_cage(col * 6, level * ______, row * 6, ______)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Your tower must have:</strong></p>
<div style="page-break-inside:avoid;break-inside:avoid;margin:14px 0">
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>#</th>
<th>Check</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>1</td>
<td>64 cages, 4 across, 4 up, 4 deep</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>2</td>
<td>an animal alive inside every cage</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>3</td>
<td>grass on the floor of every cage</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>4</td>
<td>no cage cutting through another cage</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Once the 64 stand up, keep going. Different animals on each level, or a gate you can walk through.</p>
<hr />
<h2>5 · Show Your Work 📸🎥</h2>
<p>Run your code and walk around the finished tower.</p>
<p>Record <strong>one video</strong> — one take, no stopping (a phone is fine). Show these in order:</p>
<ol>
<li>Your code on screen, and explain what each of the three loops does.</li>
<li>The tower in the world, and count a row of cages out loud.</li>
</ol>
